WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.407
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.707 --> 00:00:10.198
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:18.026
Unit thirteen: Question Forms and Question Tags. Today you will ask correct questions and confirm information.

4
00:00:18.326 --> 00:00:20.909
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:25.123
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:27.066
Question word.

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.502
Question word means a word like what or where.

8
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:32.687
What is a question word.

9
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:36.029
Your turn. Say: Question word.

10
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:40.030
Question word.

11
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:41.982
Auxiliary.

12
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.877
Auxiliary means a helping verb like do or have.

13
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:47.960
Do is an auxiliary.

14
00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.063
Your turn. Say: Auxiliary.

15
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.075
Auxiliary.

16
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:57.329
Subject question.

17
00:00:58.317 --> 00:01:01.756
Subject question means a question that asks about the subject.

18
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.595
Who called you?

19
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:07.149
Your turn. Say: Subject question.

20
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.500
Subject question.

21
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.437
Tag question.

22
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.007
Tag question means a short question at the end.

23
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:18.989
You are Dara, aren't you?

24
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:22.189
Your turn. Say: Tag question.

25
00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.278
Tag question.

26
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:27.983
Negative.

27
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:30.553
Negative means with not.

28
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.639
A negative sentence.

29
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.879
Your turn. Say: Negative.

30
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:39.653
Negative.

31
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:41.313
Positive.

32
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:44.003
Positive means without not.

33
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:46.198
A positive sentence.

34
00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:49.401
Your turn. Say: Positive.

35
00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.152
Positive.

36
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:54.895
Confirm.

37
00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:58.568
Confirm means to check that something is true.

38
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:00.742
I want to confirm the date.

39
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.909
Your turn. Say: Confirm.

40
00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:07.849
Confirm.

41
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:09.677
Intonation.

42
00:02:10.683 --> 00:02:13.438
Intonation means the rise and fall of the voice.

43
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.491
A rising intonation asks a question.

44
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:20.026
Your turn. Say: Intonation.

45
00:02:22.867 --> 00:02:23.833
Intonation.

46
00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:28.412
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.691
Visal, how do we form questions?

48
00:02:32.783 --> 00:02:45.493
We put the auxiliary before the subject: Do you like music? Where does she live? In the past simple we use did, and with be we put the verb first, for example Is she tired?

49
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.432
What about subject questions?

50
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:59.776
When the question word is the subject, we do not use do or did: Who called you? What happened? We keep the same word order as a positive sentence.

51
00:03:00.883 --> 00:03:02.558
How do question tags work?

52
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:14.394
A positive sentence takes a negative tag and a negative sentence takes a positive tag: You are tired, aren't you? She doesn't like fish, does she?

53
00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:16.964
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:23.404
Grammar focus: Question: question word plus auxiliary plus subject plus verb.

55
00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:24.891
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:27.037
Where does she live?

57
00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.532
She is tired, isn't she?

58
00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:39.098
Use an auxiliary before the subject in questions. In tags, use a negative tag after a positive sentence and a positive tag after a negative one.

59
00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.758
Be careful! Don't say: Where she lives?

60
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.073
Say: Where does she live?

61
00:03:46.373 --> 00:03:47.885
Use an auxiliary.

62
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.248
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.499
Asking Questions.

64
00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.634
A teacher asks, Who called you last night?

65
00:03:57.633 --> 00:03:59.668
Dara answers that it was his cousin.

66
00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.119
She asks, Where does your cousin live?

67
00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.144
He lives in Battambang, doesn't he?

68
00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.446
The teacher says, You don't like fish, do you?

69
00:04:10.533 --> 00:04:14.489
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.734
Where blank she live?

71
00:04:17.034 --> 00:04:19.759
A, is. B, does. C, do.

72
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.671
The answer is B: does.

73
00:04:26.817 --> 00:04:28.108
She is tired, blank?

74
00:04:28.408 --> 00:04:32.259
A, is she. B, doesn't she. C, isn't she.

75
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.869
The answer is C: isn't she.

76
00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:41.193
Who called you? uses blank.

77
00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:45.007
A, no do or did. B, do. C, did.

78
00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.240
The answer is A: no do or did.

79
00:04:52.383 --> 00:04:54.081
He doesn't like fish, blank?

80
00:04:54.381 --> 00:04:58.151
A, isn't he. B, does he. C, doesn't he.

81
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.444
The answer is B: does he.

82
00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:06.246
Where does Dara's cousin live?

83
00:05:06.546 --> 00:05:10.142
A, Phnom Penh. B, Siem Reap. C, Battambang.

84
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.491
The answer is C: Battambang.

85
00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.119
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:23.296
Ask me two questions about my school.

87
00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:33.491
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:41.995
What time does your school start in the morning? You study English every day, don't you? I would also like to ask what your favourite subject is.

89
00:05:42.295 --> 00:05:43.865
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:51.744
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and question: question word plus auxiliary plus subject plus verb.

91
00:05:52.044 --> 00:05:55.939
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

92
00:05:56.239 --> 00:05:59.147
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:59.447 --> 00:06:01.821
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

